  "id": "COMPOUND:36961 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2-Carbomethoxy-9,10-anthraquinone and Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5, through a series of target interactions. This compound is implicated in the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is known to modify histone proteins, particularly at lysine 9 of histone H3, a critical step in gene regulation. The evidence indicates that 2-Carbomethoxy-9,10-anthraquinone acts as a target of multiple compounds, including (+)-Phylliroside, quillaic acid, and Dimethyl 3-hydroxyphthalate, all of which are associated with the same target complex. These compounds are likely to exert their effects by modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, thereby influencing histone methylation. The consistent involvement of this complex in the regulation of histone H3 lysine 9 methylation suggests a mechanistic link between the compound and the target enzyme. The evidence is robust and supports a pathway where 2-Carbomethoxy-9,10-anthraquinone may influence histone methylation through its interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially affecting gene expression.",
